            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Receptacles

- All exterior doors

- From the basement

- Furnace chimney

- Furnace combustion air



During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.





</airSeal>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-30. The insulation is composed by 2 layers of 6?????????????????? fiberglass batt insulation with an insulation value of R-20/each. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Have you already thought about having a heat pump? This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However, this kind of system can?????????t operate on temperature below -25 degrees Celsius, it then will require a secondary system to maintain the heat. In this case, the furnace can ensure the heat and the ducting system can be used by the heat pump to supply heat in the entire building. You might be eligible to participate in the Heat Pumps pilot project, please follow the link below for more information;

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available



</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
